                            <comment id="498408" author="adilger" created="Thu, 23 Jul 2026 17:09:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;On failures that I looked at I saw on the OSS console:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[23034.214931] LustreError: 1020912:0:(ofd_dev.c:1775:ofd_create_hdl()) lustre-OST0000: unable to precreate: rc = -28
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;but the &lt;tt&gt;createmany&lt;/tt&gt; process doesn&apos;t report an error and is still running at the end of the test.  It seems like the &lt;tt&gt;&amp;#45;ENOSPC&lt;/tt&gt; object precreate error is being lost by the MDS and never returned to the client, or the MDS is waiting on the precreate after it already failed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
